conservative icon rush limbaugh was laid  to rest this wednesday after losing his  battle with lung cancer  it's coincidental but fitting that he  was buried this week during cpac a time  when conservatives come together  and celebrate and lay the groundwork for  the future of the republican party  rush has a special place in cpac lore he  gave a rousing speech there in 2009 as  president obama had just taken office  and the democrats had control of the  house and senate the gop  felt like it was reeling and rudderless  and then rush spoke and electrified the  party  we want the country to succeed and for  the country to succeed  its people its individuals must succeed  everyone among us must be pursuing  his ambition or her desire whatever with  excellence  trying to be the best they could be not  told as they are told by the democrat  party  we want every american to be the best  he or she chooses to be  we recognize we recognize that we are  all  individuals we love and revere our  founding documents the constitution and  the declaration of independence he  inspired conservatives to band together  and fight for their principles and he  inspired a generation of new  conservatives  with that speech i would know because i  was there it was my first cpac  but now russia's gone and it feels a lot  like 2009  again but a new generation of  conservatives are here to pick up his  torch  and carry on his legacy one of those  conservatives is madison cawthorne a  newly elected republican congressman  from north carolina  who gave his first speech at cpac  earlier today madison thank you for  joining us tonight  is this your first cpac or your first  speech at cpac  oh this is my first time actually coming  to see people right now i don't even  feel  i'm telling i don't not feel like i am  worthy of being compared to the great  rush limbaugh at all i'm just like you  katie he was an incredible mentor to me  myself yeah so this would have been my  11th cpac  so i'm very proud of that i learned a  lot being a young conservative there but  let's talk about you you're new in  congress  what are you learning there today and  how's the energy  who's there what's going on  well i'll tell you we're getting lots  done in congress katie uh we've actually  successfully renamed a post office  uh that's about it uh lots of progress  it is so  it is so dysfunctional in washington dc  and this is such a time when americans  actually need leadership  uh they need their representatives to be  working for them not playing politics  uh and that's all we're seeing is going  on and with nancy pelosi because why do  they even need congress when they can  just rule through executive order  so when it comes to the future of the  republican party you're obviously one of  the youngest if not the youngest  member of congress when it comes to  being a happy warrior what do you  what do you want to do what do you think  that conservatives have to do  to get back in the winning column to  take back the house maybe in 2022 you  know you can be  against the left but you also have to  provide a number of policy positions and  things for people to be hopeful for  exactly you know i think it's going back  to our founding principles and this is  not where  i believe the republican party has  veered off its course  in decades before when we actually just  started getting really involved in  social issues  uh when i think of the republican party  the the conservative movement it's all  about limited government  and that means that we are truly focused  on making sure that we're going to  defend our liberties we're going to make  sure we have a great moral foundation to  stand upon  and we're going to use all of that to  create an incredible economy and an  incredible country  that requires very little governance  because it's a moral people and they can  govern themselves so i think taking that  message to a new generation  that's been deceived by this outrage  culture that's been told that  conservatives are are racist or are  bigoted that can't be further from the  truth we are the big tent party but are  also  the party that welcomes diversity of  thought we want to have a debate with  you we don't want to cancel you  so you brought up the idea of people  governing themselves and that's  certainly a bedrock a conservative  principle but in your speech today you  talk specifically about  personal responsibility being  responsible for your own actions and  being capable of doing that in order to  move yourself forward so that everybody  can live their own lives and live  live out the way that they want to so  how do you get that message back into  your generation when a lot of us been  taught that  you know personal responsibility is not  really something you have to  take on board oh you're absolutely right  the  the way that we do this is by packaging  the message of  personal responsibility in a way that  makes sense uh and it's one that you  know  it encourages people and inspires people  to rise up to be a conservative  uh this should be the highest standard  in all of society not just a low bar  saying oh well if you believe in liberty  you can you can join our party no  if you want to be a millionaire you can  be in our party if you want to  live the most successful life you  possibly can you want to lead a ministry  if you want to run a non-profit  come to our party we're going to have  deregulation we're going to allow you to  live your life on your own terms  get rid of capital gains taxes get rid  of taxes across again  a federal income tax across the board so  that you have more of your own money in  your pocket this is things that  everybody can understand  and katie i think the really bedrock  principle we need to get back to  is dining room politics all politics are  local  if we are speaking to those young  families who are sitting around their  dinner table  and affecting change in the areas that  actually matter to them  then that's going to that's going to  bring the the new next generation back  to our party  so when it comes to you know bringing  we're a big it's a republican party as a  big ten party it's certainly expanded  under president trump when it comes to  just again  taking back the narrative when it comes  to the left saying that it's a party of  white supremacists and and bigots and  it's not a big tent party  how do you not just make statements but  get people to  change their votes and their party  affiliation  well you know what i think it's meeting  them where they are uh you know if you  sit  in bubbles that are completely  conservative your entire life uh you're  probably never gonna get to effect  change uh with a moderate or with a  liberal  uh but you know i think if people are  willing to have conversations again  instead of canceling your neighbor  communicate with them  and you know go have conversations with  people who disagree with you and we have  the common sense policies that actually  make sense  uh so instead of just going for the  jugular attacking people on personal  levels  if we were to actually get people to  come together and have a conversation i  think we would see  hoards of people come to the republican  party but unfortunately that's the exact  opposite of what the democrats want to  do you saw  the two of my colleagues authored a  letter trying to cancel this entire news  station  lots of letters from democrats uh and  censorship that's for sure so madison  cawthorn thank you for joining us on  your voyage journey to cpac have a great  time  it's it's very fun you'll be addicted  now i guarantee there'll be more of them  in your future thank you thank you
 

